  "text": "We're an independent act out of Richmond, Virginia, and we've put together a 12-stop run across 12 days and 1,936 total miles that we think fits rooms on your roster well. For fans of Big Thief, Waxahatchee, and Adrianne Lenker, the routing is based on Qloo taste affinities, and it skips the usual big-city circuit entirely: none of our stops overlap with the standard major markets, and nine of the twelve are over-index towns where listeners like ours show up stronger than you'd expect. The loop opens at The Jefferson Theater in Charlottesville and The Golden Pony in Harrisonburg, swings out through Pittsburgh, Columbus, and Bloomington, then works back down through The Grey Eagle in Asheville, 40 Watt Club in Athens, Georgia, and closes at Cat's Cradle in Carrboro. Every leg is a show day with no lost drive days, and the core audience at most stops reads 30 to 34. We'd love to talk about making it happen.",
